# graphs/ai-readiness: a squiddy graph (squiddy SQ-019). The rules are arnold's for its graphs (arnold/.gitignore,
# the KG-001 block), scoped to this directory: the ledger, manifest, spec, configs, candidates and evidence records are
# tracked; bulky or local artifacts (texts, exports, the adopted extraction records, which the adopter rebuilds
# deterministically from ai-readiness-kg's event log, the served query log) are not.
corpus/*
!corpus/manifest.yaml
!corpus/candidates/
!corpus/manifest_property_allowlist.yaml
!corpus/identifier_abstentions.jsonl
ledger/*.bak-*
ledger/snapshots/
exports/*.json
exports/*.jsonl
evidence/*/*.rows.jsonl
work/
texts/
extract/records/
extract/raw/
extract/meter.jsonl
extract/daemon.*
factory/queries.jsonl
__pycache__/
# R-212: a file dropped in the inbox is a document, held where it lands like ai-readiness-kg's corpus files (whose
# bytes stay local and whose provenance is the catalog); the directory itself is kept by its .gitkeep
intake/inbox/*
!intake/inbox/.gitkeep
